        {
          "path": "Project/Starting brief",
          "content": "Kitchen refit at 19 Maple Terrace, November 2026. I keep living in the house throughout.\nScope: refit the sink-wall base cabinets and the two wall cabinets beside the window with five new made-to-measure doors and new concealed hinges; two GFCI countertop receptacles and a dedicated 20 A microwave circuit. No structural work: no walls, plumbing runs or gas lines are moved.\nBudget: $3,200 for the whole project, doors included.\nHouse rules: work on weekdays in daylight; the sink is reconnected and usable every evening.\nHardware and sizes come from the drawing Kerry and I signed on Oct 30.",
          "created_at": "2026-10-12T20:30:00",
          "modified_at": "2026-10-30T21:05:00"
        },
        {
          "path": "Project/Budget",
          "content": "Kitchen refit budget (cap $3,200)\nDoors: five made-to-measure shaker doors, $1,180, paid by card Oct 20, delivered Oct 26\nKitchen design and drawing (Kerry Lin): $450, paid Oct 30 from the design fund, not part of the refit cap\nCabinet fitting: to be chosen\nElectrical (Spark Check Electric): $560 quoted, permit included\nHinges: to be ordered from the signed drawing",
          "created_at": "2026-10-12T20:40:00",
          "modified_at": "2026-10-30T21:10:00"
        },
        {
          "path": "Project/Quote - Oak Fit Cabinetry v2 (Oct 28).pdf",
          "content": "Oak Fit Cabinetry, Sacramento. Contractor's license 1084417, classification C-6 cabinet, millwork and finish carpentry, active.\nQuote OF-2611 rev. 2, Oct 28 2026, for Priya Shah, 19 Maple Terrace. Replaces rev. 1 of Oct 14.\nScope: remove and refit the sink-wall base cabinets and two wall cabinets; hang five customer-supplied doors on customer-supplied hinges per the signed drawing; adjust and clean up. Labour only: $920.\nPayment: deposit $92 (10%) on signing; balance $828 when the customer signs the completion sheet. No other charges.\nSchedule: a site survey before fitting; fitting in one weekday visit after the electrical inspection has passed and the hinges are on site; sink reconnected by 17:00. Adjustments within 30 days at no charge.",
          "created_at": "2026-10-28T16:20:00",
          "modified_at": "2026-10-28T16:20:00"
        },
        {
          "path": "Project/Quote - Oak Fit Cabinetry v1 (Oct 14).pdf",
          "content": "Oak Fit Cabinetry. Quote OF-2611 rev. 1, Oct 14 2026. Scope: refit base and wall cabinets, hang six doors including the corner door. Labour only: $980. Deposit $98 on signing; balance on completion. Superseded by rev. 2.",
          "created_at": "2026-10-14T11:05:00",
          "modified_at": "2026-10-14T11:05:00"
        },
        {
          "path": "Project/Quote - Pine Build.pdf",
          "content": "Pine Build, Elk Grove. Quote PB-0417, Oct 29 2026, for Priya Shah. Scope: refit cabinets and hang five doors. Labour $1,100. Terms: 50% ($550) on signing to reserve the November slot, 50% on completion. Contractor's license: application pending.",
          "created_at": "2026-10-29T09:40:00",
          "modified_at": "2026-10-29T09:40:00"
        },
        {
          "path": "Project/Electrical quote - Spark Check Electric.pdf",
          "content": "Spark Check Electric, contractor's license C-10, active. Quote SC-3307, Oct 27 2026.\nScope: replace the two countertop receptacles by the sink with GFCI receptacles; add a dedicated 20 A circuit for the microwave; pull and close the City of Sacramento electrical permit.\nPrice: $560 including the permit fee. Payment in full once the city inspection has passed. Cabinets must not cover the new boxes until then.",
          "created_at": "2026-10-27T15:00:00",
          "modified_at": "2026-10-27T15:00:00"
        },
        {
          "path": "Project/Cabinet drawing - signed Oct 30.pdf",
          "content": "Kitchen cabinet drawing KL-118, signed Oct 30 2026 by Priya Shah (owner) and Kerry Lin (designer).\nCabinets: existing frameless boxes, 18 mm door thickness.\nDoors: five (two base doors by the sink, one base door left of the dishwasher, two wall doors by the window). Corner door removed from scope.\nHinges: concealed, 35 mm cup, 110 degree, full overlay, soft-close, for frameless cabinets; two per door, ten in total. Hardware part H35-A (one pack of 5 pairs).\nNo change to the sink, plumbing or walls.",
